      "raw_text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 2 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Low Pressure Area (LPA)\nIssued at: 5:00 AM, 26 August 2025(Tuesday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Quezon.\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate rains over Bulacan, Bataan, Pampanga, Nueva Ecija and Zambales within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Laguna, Batangas, Cavite, Metro Manila and Rizal which may persist within 3 hours.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 8:00 AM today.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
      "cleaned_text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 2 #NCR_PRSD Weather System: Low Pressure Area (LPA) Issued at: 5:00 AM, 26 August 2025(Tuesday) YELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Quezon. ASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas. Meanwhile, expect light to moderate rains over Bulacan, Bataan, Pampanga, Nueva Ecija and Zambales within the next 3 hours. Light to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Laguna, Batangas, Cavite, Metro Manila and Rizal which may persist within 3 hours. The public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 8:00 AM today. For more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to",
      "english_translation": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 2 #NCR_PRSD Weather System: Low Pressure Area (LPA) Issued at: 5:00 AM, 26 August 2025(Tuesday) YELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Quezon. ASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas. Meanwhile, expect light to moderate rains over Bulacan, Bataan, Pampanga, Nueva Ecija and Zambales within the next 3 hours. Light to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Laguna, Batangas, Cavite, Metro Manila and Rizal which may persist within 3 hours. The public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 8:00 AM today. For more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to",
